---
title: Lazy Tool Discovery
id: lazy-tool-discovery
order: 6
description: "Reduce token cost in tool-heavy TanStack AI apps with lazy tool discovery — the LLM discovers only the tools it needs for the current task."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - lazy tools
  - tool discovery
  - token optimization
  - context optimization
  - performance
  - large tool sets
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When an application has many tools, sending all tool definitions to the LLM on every request wastes tokens and can degrade response quality. Lazy tool discovery lets the LLM selectively discover only the tools it needs for the current task."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-it-works","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How It Works"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools marked with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lazy: true"},{"type":"text","value":" are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" sent to the LLM upfront. Instead, a synthetic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__lazy__tool__discovery__"},{"type":"text","value":" tool is created whose description lists all available lazy tool names. The LLM can call this discovery tool with the names of tools it wants to learn about, and receives their full descriptions and argument schemas in return."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once discovered, lazy tools are dynamically injected as normal tools — the LLM calls them directly like any other tool."}]},{"type":"code","value":"sequenceDiagram\n    participant LLM\n    participant Server\n    participant Discovery Tool\n    participant Lazy Tool\n\n    Note over LLM: Sees __lazy__tool__discovery__<br/>with available tool names\n\n    LLM->>Server: Call __lazy__tool__discovery__<br/>{toolNames: [\"searchProducts\"]}\n    Server->>Discovery Tool: Execute discovery\n    Discovery Tool-->>Server: Return description + schema\n    Server-->>LLM: Tool result with schema\n\n    Note over LLM: searchProducts now available<br/>as a normal tool\n\n    LLM->>Server: Call searchProducts<br/>{query: \"red shoes\"}\n    Server->>Lazy Tool: Execute searchProducts\n    Lazy Tool-->>Server: Return results\n    Server-->>LLM: Tool result","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"marking-tools-as-lazy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marking Tools as Lazy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lazy: true"},{"type":"text","value":" to any tool definition:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition, chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\nimport { getProducts, compareProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst searchProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"searchProducts\",\n  description: \"Search products by keyword in name or description\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    query: z.string().describe(\"Search keyword or phrase\"),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    results: z.array(\n      z.object({\n        id: z.number(),\n        name: z.string(),\n        price: z.number(),\n      })\n    ),\n  }),\n  lazy: true, // This tool won't be sent to the LLM upfront\n});\n\nconst searchProducts = searchProductsDef.server(async ({ query }) => {\n  const results = await db.products.search(query);\n  return { results };\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=lazy-intro"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" alongside your other tools:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"async function handleRequest(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      getProducts, // Normal tool — sent to LLM immediately\n      searchProducts, // Lazy tool — discovered on demand\n      compareProducts, // Lazy tool — discovered on demand\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=lazy-intro"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"controlling-the-discovery-catalog","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Controlling the Discovery Catalog"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__lazy__tool__discovery__"},{"type":"text","value":" tool's description lists only the\n"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"names"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of available lazy tools. The optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lazyToolsConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"\ncontrols how much of each lazy tool's description appears in that pre-discovery\ncatalog:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { getProducts, searchProducts, compareProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nasync function handleRequest(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getProducts, searchProducts, compareProducts],\n    lazyToolsConfig: {\n      // 'none' (default) | 'first-sentence' | 'full'\n      includeDescription: \"first-sentence\",\n    },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includeDescription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Catalog entry for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"searchProducts"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'none'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"searchProducts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'first-sentence'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"searchProducts — Search products by keyword."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'full'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"searchProducts — <full description>"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This only affects the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pre-discovery"}]},{"type":"text","value":" catalog. Regardless of the setting, the\ndiscovery tool's result always returns each tool's full description and argument\nschema — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includeDescription"},{"type":"text","value":" just tunes how much the LLM sees before it\ndecides what to discover. The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'none'"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the catalog as lean as\npossible."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lazyToolsConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional and the same option is accepted by Code Mode's\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCodeMode()"},{"type":"text","value":" — see "},{"type":"link","href":"../code-mode/lazy-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode Lazy Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-lazy-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to Use Lazy Tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lazy tools are useful when:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have many tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and want to reduce token usage per request"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some tools are rarely needed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — secondary features like comparison, financing, or advanced search"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool descriptions are large"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — lazy tools keep the initial prompt lean"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools that are called in most conversations should remain eager (the default)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"discovery-flow","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discovery Flow"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The LLM sees "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__lazy__tool__discovery__"},{"type":"text","value":" with a list of available tool names in its description"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Based on the user's request, the LLM decides which tools it needs and calls the discovery tool"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The discovery tool returns the full description and JSON Schema for each requested tool"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The discovered tools are injected as normal tools for the next iteration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The LLM calls the discovered tools directly"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The LLM can discover one or many tools in a single call:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// LLM calls:\n__lazy__tool__discovery__({ toolNames: [\"searchProducts\", \"compareProducts\"] })"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"multi-turn-conversations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multi-Turn Conversations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lazy tool discovery works across multiple turns. When a tool is discovered in one turn, it remains available in subsequent turns within the same conversation — the LLM does not need to re-discover it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is handled automatically by scanning the message history for previous discovery tool results on each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"self-correction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Self-Correction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the LLM tries to call a lazy tool that hasn't been discovered yet, it receives an error message:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Error: Tool 'searchProducts' must be discovered first.\nCall __lazy__tool__discovery__ with toolNames: ['searchProducts'] to discover it."},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The LLM then self-corrects by calling the discovery tool first, then retrying the original tool call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"zero-overhead","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Zero Overhead"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If none of your tools have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lazy: true"},{"type":"text","value":", no discovery tool is created and the behavior is identical to the default. There is no performance or token cost when lazy discovery is not in use."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When all lazy tools have been discovered, the discovery tool is automatically removed from the active tool set."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here's a complete example with a mix of eager and lazy tools:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition, chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, maxIterations } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\n// Eager tool — always available\nconst getProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"getProducts\",\n  description: \"Get all products from the catalog\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  outputSchema: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      id: z.number(),\n      name: z.string(),\n      price: z.number(),\n    })\n  ),\n});\n\nconst getProducts = getProductsDef.server(async () => {\n  return await db.products.findMany();\n});\n\n// Lazy tool — discovered on demand\nconst compareProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"compareProducts\",\n  description: \"Compare two or more products side by side\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    productIds: z.array(z.number()).min(2),\n  }),\n  lazy: true,\n});\n\nconst compareProducts = compareProductsDef.server(async ({ productIds }) => {\n  const products = await db.products.findMany({\n    where: { id: { in: productIds } },\n  });\n  return { products };\n});\n\n// Lazy tool — discovered on demand\nconst calculateFinancingDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"calculateFinancing\",\n  description: \"Calculate monthly payment plans for a product\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    productId: z.number(),\n    months: z.number(),\n  }),\n  lazy: true,\n});\n\nconst calculateFinancing = calculateFinancingDef.server(async ({ productId, months }) => {\n  const product = await db.products.findUnique({ where: { id: productId } });\n  const monthlyPayment = product.price / months;\n  return { monthlyPayment, totalPrice: product.price, months };\n});\n\n// Use in chat\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getProducts, compareProducts, calculateFinancing],\n    agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(20),\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With this setup:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The LLM always sees "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getProducts"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__lazy__tool__discovery__"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a user asks to compare products, the LLM discovers "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compareProducts"},{"type":"text","value":" first, then calls it"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a user asks about financing, the LLM discovers "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"calculateFinancing"},{"type":"text","value":" first, then calls it"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Basic tool concepts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./server-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Server-side tool execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./tool-architecture","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool Architecture"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Deep dive into the tool system"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../chat/agentic-cycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agentic Cycle"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - How the agent loop works"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"how-it-works","text":"How It Works","level":2},{"id":"marking-tools-as-lazy","text":"Marking Tools as Lazy","level":2},{"id":"controlling-the-discovery-catalog","text":"Controlling the Discovery Catalog","level":2},{"id":"when-to-use-lazy-tools","text":"When to Use Lazy Tools","level":2},{"id":"discovery-flow","text":"Discovery Flow","level":2},{"id":"multi-turn-conversations","text":"Multi-Turn Conversations","level":2},{"id":"self-correction","text":"Self-Correction","level":2},{"id":"zero-overhead","text":"Zero Overhead","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWhen an application has many tools, sending all tool definitions to the LLM on every request wastes tokens and can degrade response quality. Lazy tool discovery lets the LLM selectively discover only the tools it needs for the current task.\n\n## How It Works\n\nTools marked with `lazy: true` are **not** sent to the LLM upfront. Instead, a synthetic `__lazy__tool__discovery__` tool is created whose description lists all available lazy tool names. The LLM can call this discovery tool with the names of tools it wants to learn about, and receives their full descriptions and argument schemas in return.\n\nOnce discovered, lazy tools are dynamically injected as normal tools — the LLM calls them directly like any other tool.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant LLM\n    participant Server\n    participant Discovery Tool\n    participant Lazy Tool\n\n    Note over LLM: Sees __lazy__tool__discovery__<br/>with available tool names\n\n    LLM->>Server: Call __lazy__tool__discovery__<br/>{toolNames: [\"searchProducts\"]}\n    Server->>Discovery Tool: Execute discovery\n    Discovery Tool-->>Server: Return description + schema\n    Server-->>LLM: Tool result with schema\n\n    Note over LLM: searchProducts now available<br/>as a normal tool\n\n    LLM->>Server: Call searchProducts<br/>{query: \"red shoes\"}\n    Server->>Lazy Tool: Execute searchProducts\n    Lazy Tool-->>Server: Return results\n    Server-->>LLM: Tool result\n```\n\n## Marking Tools as Lazy\n\nAdd `lazy: true` to any tool definition:\n\n```typescript group=lazy-intro\nimport { toolDefinition, chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\nimport { getProducts, compareProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst searchProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"searchProducts\",\n  description: \"Search products by keyword in name or description\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    query: z.string().describe(\"Search keyword or phrase\"),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    results: z.array(\n      z.object({\n        id: z.number(),\n        name: z.string(),\n        price: z.number(),\n      })\n    ),\n  }),\n  lazy: true, // This tool won't be sent to the LLM upfront\n});\n\nconst searchProducts = searchProductsDef.server(async ({ query }) => {\n  const results = await db.products.search(query);\n  return { results };\n});\n```\n\nThen pass it to `chat()` alongside your other tools:\n\n```typescript group=lazy-intro\nasync function handleRequest(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      getProducts, // Normal tool — sent to LLM immediately\n      searchProducts, // Lazy tool — discovered on demand\n      compareProducts, // Lazy tool — discovered on demand\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Controlling the Discovery Catalog\n\nBy default, the `__lazy__tool__discovery__` tool's description lists only the\n**names** of available lazy tools. The optional `lazyToolsConfig` on `chat()`\ncontrols how much of each lazy tool's description appears in that pre-discovery\ncatalog:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { getProducts, searchProducts, compareProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nasync function handleRequest(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getProducts, searchProducts, compareProducts],\n    lazyToolsConfig: {\n      // 'none' (default) | 'first-sentence' | 'full'\n      includeDescription: \"first-sentence\",\n    },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n| `includeDescription` | Catalog entry for `searchProducts`              |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `'none'` (default)   | `searchProducts`                                |\n| `'first-sentence'`   | `searchProducts — Search products by keyword.`  |\n| `'full'`             | `searchProducts — <full description>`           |\n\nThis only affects the **pre-discovery** catalog. Regardless of the setting, the\ndiscovery tool's result always returns each tool's full description and argument\nschema — `includeDescription` just tunes how much the LLM sees before it\ndecides what to discover. The default `'none'` keeps the catalog as lean as\npossible.\n\n`lazyToolsConfig` is optional and the same option is accepted by Code Mode's\n`createCodeMode()` — see [Code Mode Lazy Tools](../code-mode/lazy-tools).\n\n## When to Use Lazy Tools\n\nLazy tools are useful when:\n\n- **You have many tools** and want to reduce token usage per request\n- **Some tools are rarely needed** — secondary features like comparison, financing, or advanced search\n- **Tool descriptions are large** — lazy tools keep the initial prompt lean\n\nTools that are called in most conversations should remain eager (the default).\n\n## Discovery Flow\n\n1. The LLM sees `__lazy__tool__discovery__` with a list of available tool names in its description\n2. Based on the user's request, the LLM decides which tools it needs and calls the discovery tool\n3. The discovery tool returns the full description and JSON Schema for each requested tool\n4. The discovered tools are injected as normal tools for the next iteration\n5. The LLM calls the discovered tools directly\n\nThe LLM can discover one or many tools in a single call:\n\n```\n// LLM calls:\n__lazy__tool__discovery__({ toolNames: [\"searchProducts\", \"compareProducts\"] })\n```\n\n## Multi-Turn Conversations\n\nLazy tool discovery works across multiple turns. When a tool is discovered in one turn, it remains available in subsequent turns within the same conversation — the LLM does not need to re-discover it.\n\nThis is handled automatically by scanning the message history for previous discovery tool results on each `chat()` call.\n\n## Self-Correction\n\nIf the LLM tries to call a lazy tool that hasn't been discovered yet, it receives an error message:\n\n```\nError: Tool 'searchProducts' must be discovered first.\nCall __lazy__tool__discovery__ with toolNames: ['searchProducts'] to discover it.\n```\n\nThe LLM then self-corrects by calling the discovery tool first, then retrying the original tool call.\n\n## Zero Overhead\n\nIf none of your tools have `lazy: true`, no discovery tool is created and the behavior is identical to the default. There is no performance or token cost when lazy discovery is not in use.\n\nWhen all lazy tools have been discovered, the discovery tool is automatically removed from the active tool set.\n\n## Example\n\nHere's a complete example with a mix of eager and lazy tools:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition, chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, maxIterations } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\n// Eager tool — always available\nconst getProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"getProducts\",\n  description: \"Get all products from the catalog\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  outputSchema: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      id: z.number(),\n      name: z.string(),\n      price: z.number(),\n    })\n  ),\n});\n\nconst getProducts = getProductsDef.server(async () => {\n  return await db.products.findMany();\n});\n\n// Lazy tool — discovered on demand\nconst compareProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"compareProducts\",\n  description: \"Compare two or more products side by side\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    productIds: z.array(z.number()).min(2),\n  }),\n  lazy: true,\n});\n\nconst compareProducts = compareProductsDef.server(async ({ productIds }) => {\n  const products = await db.products.findMany({\n    where: { id: { in: productIds } },\n  });\n  return { products };\n});\n\n// Lazy tool — discovered on demand\nconst calculateFinancingDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"calculateFinancing\",\n  description: \"Calculate monthly payment plans for a product\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    productId: z.number(),\n    months: z.number(),\n  }),\n  lazy: true,\n});\n\nconst calculateFinancing = calculateFinancingDef.server(async ({ productId, months }) => {\n  const product = await db.products.findUnique({ where: { id: productId } });\n  const monthlyPayment = product.price / months;\n  return { monthlyPayment, totalPrice: product.price, months };\n});\n\n// Use in chat\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getProducts, compareProducts, calculateFinancing],\n    agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(20),\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nWith this setup:\n- The LLM always sees `getProducts` and `__lazy__tool__discovery__`\n- When a user asks to compare products, the LLM discovers `compareProducts` first, then calls it\n- When a user asks about financing, the LLM discovers `calculateFinancing` first, then calls it\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Tools Overview](./tools) - Basic tool concepts\n- [Server Tools](./server-tools) - Server-side tool execution\n- [Tool Architecture](./tool-architecture) - Deep dive into the tool system\n- [Agentic Cycle](../chat/agentic-cycle) - How the agent loop works\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Lazy Tool Discovery\nid: lazy-tool-discovery\norder: 6\ndescription: \"Reduce token cost in tool-heavy TanStack AI apps with lazy tool discovery — the LLM discovers only the tools it needs for the current task.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - lazy tools\n  - tool discovery\n  - token optimization\n  - context optimization\n  - performance\n  - large tool sets\n---\n\nWhen an application has many tools, sending all tool definitions to the LLM on every request wastes tokens and can degrade response quality. Lazy tool discovery lets the LLM selectively discover only the tools it needs for the current task.\n\n## How It Works\n\nTools marked with `lazy: true` are **not** sent to the LLM upfront. Instead, a synthetic `__lazy__tool__discovery__` tool is created whose description lists all available lazy tool names. The LLM can call this discovery tool with the names of tools it wants to learn about, and receives their full descriptions and argument schemas in return.\n\nOnce discovered, lazy tools are dynamically injected as normal tools — the LLM calls them directly like any other tool.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant LLM\n    participant Server\n    participant Discovery Tool\n    participant Lazy Tool\n\n    Note over LLM: Sees __lazy__tool__discovery__<br/>with available tool names\n\n    LLM->>Server: Call __lazy__tool__discovery__<br/>{toolNames: [\"searchProducts\"]}\n    Server->>Discovery Tool: Execute discovery\n    Discovery Tool-->>Server: Return description + schema\n    Server-->>LLM: Tool result with schema\n\n    Note over LLM: searchProducts now available<br/>as a normal tool\n\n    LLM->>Server: Call searchProducts<br/>{query: \"red shoes\"}\n    Server->>Lazy Tool: Execute searchProducts\n    Lazy Tool-->>Server: Return results\n    Server-->>LLM: Tool result\n```\n\n## Marking Tools as Lazy\n\nAdd `lazy: true` to any tool definition:\n\n```typescript group=lazy-intro\nimport { toolDefinition, chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\nimport { getProducts, compareProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst searchProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"searchProducts\",\n  description: \"Search products by keyword in name or description\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    query: z.string().describe(\"Search keyword or phrase\"),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    results: z.array(\n      z.object({\n        id: z.number(),\n        name: z.string(),\n        price: z.number(),\n      })\n    ),\n  }),\n  lazy: true, // This tool won't be sent to the LLM upfront\n});\n\nconst searchProducts = searchProductsDef.server(async ({ query }) => {\n  const results = await db.products.search(query);\n  return { results };\n});\n```\n\nThen pass it to `chat()` alongside your other tools:\n\n```typescript group=lazy-intro\nasync function handleRequest(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      getProducts, // Normal tool — sent to LLM immediately\n      searchProducts, // Lazy tool — discovered on demand\n      compareProducts, // Lazy tool — discovered on demand\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Controlling the Discovery Catalog\n\nBy default, the `__lazy__tool__discovery__` tool's description lists only the\n**names** of available lazy tools. The optional `lazyToolsConfig` on `chat()`\ncontrols how much of each lazy tool's description appears in that pre-discovery\ncatalog:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { getProducts, searchProducts, compareProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nasync function handleRequest(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getProducts, searchProducts, compareProducts],\n    lazyToolsConfig: {\n      // 'none' (default) | 'first-sentence' | 'full'\n      includeDescription: \"first-sentence\",\n    },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n| `includeDescription` | Catalog entry for `searchProducts`              |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `'none'` (default)   | `searchProducts`                                |\n| `'first-sentence'`   | `searchProducts — Search products by keyword.`  |\n| `'full'`             | `searchProducts — <full description>`           |\n\nThis only affects the **pre-discovery** catalog. Regardless of the setting, the\ndiscovery tool's result always returns each tool's full description and argument\nschema — `includeDescription` just tunes how much the LLM sees before it\ndecides what to discover. The default `'none'` keeps the catalog as lean as\npossible.\n\n`lazyToolsConfig` is optional and the same option is accepted by Code Mode's\n`createCodeMode()` — see [Code Mode Lazy Tools](../code-mode/lazy-tools).\n\n## When to Use Lazy Tools\n\nLazy tools are useful when:\n\n- **You have many tools** and want to reduce token usage per request\n- **Some tools are rarely needed** — secondary features like comparison, financing, or advanced search\n- **Tool descriptions are large** — lazy tools keep the initial prompt lean\n\nTools that are called in most conversations should remain eager (the default).\n\n## Discovery Flow\n\n1. The LLM sees `__lazy__tool__discovery__` with a list of available tool names in its description\n2. Based on the user's request, the LLM decides which tools it needs and calls the discovery tool\n3. The discovery tool returns the full description and JSON Schema for each requested tool\n4. The discovered tools are injected as normal tools for the next iteration\n5. The LLM calls the discovered tools directly\n\nThe LLM can discover one or many tools in a single call:\n\n```\n// LLM calls:\n__lazy__tool__discovery__({ toolNames: [\"searchProducts\", \"compareProducts\"] })\n```\n\n## Multi-Turn Conversations\n\nLazy tool discovery works across multiple turns. When a tool is discovered in one turn, it remains available in subsequent turns within the same conversation — the LLM does not need to re-discover it.\n\nThis is handled automatically by scanning the message history for previous discovery tool results on each `chat()` call.\n\n## Self-Correction\n\nIf the LLM tries to call a lazy tool that hasn't been discovered yet, it receives an error message:\n\n```\nError: Tool 'searchProducts' must be discovered first.\nCall __lazy__tool__discovery__ with toolNames: ['searchProducts'] to discover it.\n```\n\nThe LLM then self-corrects by calling the discovery tool first, then retrying the original tool call.\n\n## Zero Overhead\n\nIf none of your tools have `lazy: true`, no discovery tool is created and the behavior is identical to the default. There is no performance or token cost when lazy discovery is not in use.\n\nWhen all lazy tools have been discovered, the discovery tool is automatically removed from the active tool set.\n\n## Example\n\nHere's a complete example with a mix of eager and lazy tools:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition, chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, maxIterations } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\n// Eager tool — always available\nconst getProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"getProducts\",\n  description: \"Get all products from the catalog\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  outputSchema: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      id: z.number(),\n      name: z.string(),\n      price: z.number(),\n    })\n  ),\n});\n\nconst getProducts = getProductsDef.server(async () => {\n  return await db.products.findMany();\n});\n\n// Lazy tool — discovered on demand\nconst compareProductsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"compareProducts\",\n  description: \"Compare two or more products side by side\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    productIds: z.array(z.number()).min(2),\n  }),\n  lazy: true,\n});\n\nconst compareProducts = compareProductsDef.server(async ({ productIds }) => {\n  const products = await db.products.findMany({\n    where: { id: { in: productIds } },\n  });\n  return { products };\n});\n\n// Lazy tool — discovered on demand\nconst calculateFinancingDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"calculateFinancing\",\n  description: \"Calculate monthly payment plans for a product\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    productId: z.number(),\n    months: z.number(),\n  }),\n  lazy: true,\n});\n\nconst calculateFinancing = calculateFinancingDef.server(async ({ productId, months }) => {\n  const product = await db.products.findUnique({ where: { id: productId } });\n  const monthlyPayment = product.price / months;\n  return { monthlyPayment, totalPrice: product.price, months };\n});\n\n// Use in chat\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getProducts, compareProducts, calculateFinancing],\n    agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(20),\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nWith this setup:\n- The LLM always sees `getProducts` and `__lazy__tool__discovery__`\n- When a user asks to compare products, the LLM discovers `compareProducts` first, then calls it\n- When a user asks about financing, the LLM discovers `calculateFinancing` first, then calls it\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Tools Overview](./tools) - Basic tool concepts\n- [Server Tools](./server-tools) - Server-side tool execution\n- [Tool Architecture](./tool-architecture) - Deep dive into the tool system\n- [Agentic Cycle](../chat/agentic-cycle) - How the agent loop works\n"}
